# Copy to .env.local (Vite ignores it by default; do not commit real values).
# Optional. The help coach works fully offline without this — it is only used
# as a fallback when a typed question matches none of coach.js's local
# patterns. Leave blank to keep the coach 100% local, no backend, no network.
#
# Set this to the ClassifyIntentUrl output from `cdk deploy` in backend/.
VITE_CLASSIFY_INTENT_URL=

# Optional, and independent of the line above. The last-resort coach tier: when
# a typed question matches no local pattern AND the classifier places no
# existing answer, this lets a model read the position and answer in its own
# words. Fenced (backend builds the facts, reply is length-checked, any failure
# drops to the offline coach) but, unlike the classifier, it does write the
# text the player reads. Set it to the CoachAnswerUrl output from `cdk deploy`.
VITE_COACH_ANSWER_URL=

# Optional. The post-hand review panel works fully offline without this (a plain
# summary computed from the hand's own decision log). Set it to the ReviewHandUrl
# output from `cdk deploy` in backend/ to have a cheap Bedrock model phrase that
# summary more warmly. Any failure falls back to the offline version.
VITE_REVIEW_URL=
